"","v":[10,11,12,13]},{"id":"salah_2455","name":"Salah","also":"Shelah","summary":"A shoot, a descendant of Arphaxed (Luke 3:35, 36); called also Shelah (1 Chr. 1:18, 24).","verses":8,"father":"Cainan","mother":"","v":[12,13,14,15]},{"id":"eber_1030","name":"Eber","also":"Heber","summary":"The third post-duluvian patriach after Shem (Gen. 10:24; 11:14). He is regarded as the founder of the Hebrew race (10:21; Num. 24:24).","verses":12,"father":"Salah","mother":"","v":[14,15,16,17]},{"id":"peleg_2308","name":"Peleg","also":"Phalec","summary":"Division, one of the sons of Eber; so called because “in his days was the earth divided” (Gen. 10:25). Possibly he may have lived at the time of the dispersion from Babel.","verses":8,"father":"Eber","mother":"","v":[16,17,18,19]},{"id":"reu_2428","name":"Reu","also":"Ragau","summary":"","verses":6,"father":"Peleg","mother":"","v":[18,19,20,21]},{"id":"serug_2503","name":"Serug","also":"Saruch","summary":"Branch, the father of Nahor (Gen. 11:20-23); called Saruch in Luke 3:35.","verses":6,"father":"Reu","mother":"","v":[20,21,22,23]},{"id":"nahor_2142","name":"Nahor","also":"Nachor","summary":"The father of Terah, who was the father of Abraham (Gen. 11:22-25; Luke 3:34).","verses":7,"father":"Serug","mother":"","v":[22,23,24,25]},{"id":"terah_2841","name":"Terah","also":"Thara","summary":"The wanderer; loiterer, for some unknown reason emigrated with his family from his native mountains in the north to the plains of Mesopotamia.","verses":10,"father":"Nahor","mother":"","v":[24,25,26,27,28,31,32]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[26,27,29,31]},{"id":"nahor_2143","name":"Nahor","also":"","summary":"A son of Terah, and elder brother of Abraham (Gen. 11:26, 27; Josh. 24:2, R.V.). He married Milcah, the daughter of his brother Haran, and remained in the land of his nativity on the east of the river Euphrates at Haran (Gen. 11:27-32).","verses":10,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[26,27,29]},{"id":"haran_1407","name":"Haran","also":"","summary":"Heb. haran; i.e., “mountaineer.” The eldest son of Terah, brother of Abraham and Nahor, and father of Lot, Milcah, and Iscah.","verses":5,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[26,27,28,29,31]},{"id":"lot_1830","name":"Lot","also":"","summary":"(Heb. goral, a “pebble”), a small stone used in casting lots (Num. 33:54; Jonah 1:7). The lot was always resorted to by the Hebrews with strictest reference to the interposition of God, and as a method of ascertaining the divine will (Prov. 16:33), and in serious cases of doubt (Esther 3:7).","verses":34,"father":"Haran","mother":"","v":[27,31]},{"id":"sarah_2473","name":"Sarah","also":"Sarai, Sara","summary":"Princess, the wife and at the same time the half-sister of Abraham (Gen. 11:29; 20:12). This name was given to her at the time that it was announced to Abraham that she should be the mother of the promised child.","verses":48,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[29,30,31]},{"id":"milcah_2082","name":"Milcah","also":"","summary":"Sister of Isca.","verses":6,"father":"Haran","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"iscah_618","name":"Iscah","also":"","summary":"Spy, the daughter of Haran and sister of Milcah and Lot (Gen. 11:29, 31).","verses":1,"father":"Haran","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"canaan_914","name":"Canaan","also":"Canaanites, Canaanite","summary":"The fourth son of Ham (Gen. 10:6). His descendants were under a curse in consequence of the transgression of his father (9:22-27). His eldest son, Zidon, was the father of the Sidonians and Phoenicians.","verses":84,"father":"Ham","mother":"","v":[31]}],"places":[{"id":"shinar_1084","name":"Shinar","kind":"Region","lat":32.5365,"lon":44.42088,"summary":"LXX. and Vulgate “Senaar;” in the inscriptions, “Shumir;” probably identical with Babylonia or Southern Mesopotamia, extending almost to the Persian Gulf.","verses":8,"v":[2]},{"id":"babel_150","name":"Babel","kind":"City","lat":32.5365,"lon":44.42088,"summary":"The name given to the tower which the primitive fathers of our race built in the land of Shinar after the Deluge (Gen. 11:1-9). Their object in building this tower was probably that it might be seen as a rallying-point in the extensive plain of Shinar, to which they had emigrated from the uplands of Armenia, and so prevent their being scattered abroad.","verses":2,"v":[9]},{"id":"ur_1189","name":"Ur","kind":"City","lat":30.9625,"lon":46.10306,"summary":"Light, or the moon city, a city “of the Chaldees,” the birthplace of Haran (Gen. 11:28, 31), the largest city of Shinar or northern Chaldea, and the principal commercial centre of the country as well as the centre of political power.","verses":4,"v":[28,31]},{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[31]},{"id":"haran_527","name":"Haran","kind":"City","lat":36.86,"lon":39.03139,"summary":"Heb. haran, i.e., “parched;” or probably from the Accadian charana, meaning “a road.” A celebrated city of Western Asia, now Harran, where Abram remained, after he left Ur of the Chaldees, till his father Terah died (Gen. 11:31, 32), when he continued his journey into the land of Canaan.","verses":10,"v":[31,32]}],"events":[{"id":"tower_of_babel_53","title":"Tower of Babel","year":-2246,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:1–9. Place: Babel.","v":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9]},{"id":"birth_of_arphaxad_45","title":"Birth of Arphaxad","year":-2346,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:10. People: Arphaxad, Shem.","v":[10]},{"id":"lifetime_of_shem_34","title":"Lifetime of Shem","year":-2446,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:10–11. People: Shem. Lasted about 600 years.","v":[10,11]},{"id":"death_of_shem_84","title":"Death of Shem","year":-1846,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:11. People: Shem.","v":[11]},{"id":"birth_of_salah_47","title":"Birth of Salah","year":-2311,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:12. People: Salah, Arphaxad.","v":[12]},{"id":"lifetime_of_arphaxad_46","title":"Lifetime of Arphaxad","year":-2346,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:12–13. People: Arphaxad. Lasted about 438 years.","v":[12,13]},{"id":"death_of_arphaxad_78","title":"Death of Arphaxad","year":-1908,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:13. People: Arphaxad.","v":[13]},{"id":"birth_of_eber_49","title":"Birth of Eber","year":-2281,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:14. People: Eber, Salah.","v":[14]},{"id":"lifetime_of_salah_48","title":"Lifetime of Salah","year":-2311,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:14–15. People: Salah. Lasted about 433 years.","v":[14,15]},{"id":"death_of_salah_82","title":"Death of Salah","year":-1878,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:15. People: Salah.","v":[15]},{"id":"birth_of_peleg_51","title":"Birth of Peleg","year":-2247,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:16. People: Peleg, Eber.","v":[16]},{"id":"lifetime_of_eber_50","title":"Lifetime of Eber","year":-2281,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:16–17. People: Eber. Lasted about 464 years.","v":[16,17]},{"id":"death_of_eber_89","title":"Death of Eber","year":-1817,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:17. People: Eber.","v":[17]},{"id":"birth_of_reu_54","title":"Birth of Reu","year":-2217,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:18. People: Reu, Peleg.","v":[18]},{"id":"lifetime_of_peleg_52","title":"Lifetime of Peleg","year":-2247,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:18–19. People: Peleg. Lasted about 239 years.","v":[18,19]},{"id":"death_of_peleg_62","title":"Death of Peleg","year":-2008,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:19. People: Peleg.","v":[19]},{"id":"birth_of_serug_56","title":"Birth of Serug","year":-2185,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:20. People: S